{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FlavorDressing.FlavorMassSplittingBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.FlavorMassSplittingBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.FlavorDressing.FlavorDressingFunctor","lean:module:QOU.FlavorDressing.DressedMassFromSubstrateSplit"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.flavor_mass_splitting_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.flavor_mass_splitting_bound","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/FlavorMassSplittingBound.lean#L149-L245","doc":"**Substrate bound on the dressed-quark splitting.**\nFor substrate parameter `q > 1`, nucleon average mass `M_N > 0`,\nand any `FlavorDressingFunctor F` satisfying the derivation\nidentity of `prop:flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split`,\nthe down–up splitting satisfies the two-sided substrate bound\n\n  0 < μ_d − μ_u < M_N · ℏ_q² · h_q · [2]_q\n\nwhere ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q, h_q = q − q⁻¹, [2]_q = q + q⁻¹.\n\nThe strict lower bound expresses positivity of the substrate\nfactor at q > 1; the strict upper bound uses the algebraic\nidentity `substrate_to_bound_ratio` plus the Skein-side\nadjustment factor `(q^{1/2}+q⁻^{1/2})/(q+q⁻¹) < 1` at q > 1.\n\n**Conditional content:** the realised value of `μ_d − μ_u`\nsits at about 1/3 of the upper bound at q = q₀; the theorem\ndoes NOT claim tightness.  Tightness would require a finer\nsubstrate factor incorporating the Skein adjustment\nexplicitly. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:flavor-mass-splitting-bound","label":"thm:flavor-mass-splitting-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-mass-splitting-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FlavorDressing.substrate_to_bound_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FlavorDressing.substrate_to_bound_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FlavorDressing/FlavorMassSplittingBound.lean#L33-L82","doc":"The substrate ratio `(q − 1)²(1 − q⁻⁴)/3` over the bound\nfactor `ℏ_q² · h_q · [2]_q` equals exactly `1/3` for any\nnon-zero `q`.  This algebraic identity is the engine of the\nupper bound; stated over a generic `Field R` per the\nrepository's base-ring convention (AGENTS.md §7c) — the\nidentity is a rational-function fact with no archimedean\ncontent.  The downstream inequality `flavor_mass_splitting_bound`\nkeeps its `ℝ` specialisation because it uses ordering.\n\nThe hypothesis `(3 : R) ≠ 0` rules out characteristic 3, where\n`1/3` itself is undefined; in `ℝ`, `ℚ`, or any char-0 field this\nis automatic. ","signatureChunk":0}]}